        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "212f6876-1774-5c0a-a9b7-ac6acf4258a4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Willunga, Adelaide, Reynella, South Australia\n- Systems: Willunga railway line, Reynella railway station, Adelaide railway station, Gawler line\n- Organizations: City of Onkaparinga\n- Topics: population, distance, rail transport\n\nFacts:\n- The Willunga railway line ran from Adelaide railway station through Adelaide’s southern suburbs to Willunga.\n- The Willunga railway line was over 45 km long, which made it longer than the current 42.2 km Gawler line.\n- Willunga is a town south of Adelaide in South Australia within the City of Onkaparinga local government area.\n- Willunga is 47 km from the Adelaide CBD.\n- At the 2011 census, Willunga had a population of 2,416.\n- Reynella railway station was a railway station in Reynella, South Australia, on the Willunga railway line.",
